WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.600
Now in the last few

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.234
minutes, the US

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.102
Secretary of Defense

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.802
said the downing

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.937
of a US spy drone

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.071
in international airspace

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.773
yesterday was part of a pattern of,

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:07.941
quote, aggressive,

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.410
risky and unsafe actions by Russia.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:11.911
Lloyd Austin's comments

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:12.712
come one day

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.446
after the Pentagon

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.647
accused a Russian fighter

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.782
jet of hitting

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.851
an American spy drones propeller,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:18.618
forcing it

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.820
to crash into international waters.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.389
But Russia's ambassador to Washington

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.223
is insisting

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.425
the incident didn't happen

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.026
and is warning

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.060
the US not to enter

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.696
the airspace as the war rages in Ukraine.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.034
This drone can carry a few booms.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.101
You'll see that.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.603
What will be the issue

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.904
of the United States?

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.740
If you'll see such a Russian drone,

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.710
very close, for example, to San Francisco

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.744
or New York?

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.212
What will the reaction

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.515
of the United States? For me, it's clear

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.818
and some Abdulaziz joins us now

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:52.352
on this summer.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.053
Perhaps no surprise

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.921
that there's a difference of opinion over

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:55.655
what happened here

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.023
given the broader backdrop.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.058
What do we know?

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.093
Firstly, about what happened?

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.294
What more happened?

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.063
What about the data on the drone

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.330
and the perhaps the communications

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.466
behind the scenes here to avoid

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.701
further escalation?

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.602
Absolutely.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.371
Two very different narratives

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.073
coming from Moscow in D.C.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.274
The United States says

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.142
that Russia intentionally hit

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.078
this drone, struck this drone

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:19.179
it says that Russian jets

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.280
were in the vicinity of it,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.181
essentially harassing

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:21.915
it between

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.383
reading between the lines for 30

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.150
to 40 minutes,

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.752
dumping fuel on that drone

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.152
before that

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.153
Russian fighter jet

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:27.787
went behind

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.823
that drone and clipped its propeller.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:30.490
The drone

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.192
then that reaper drone

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.227
being forced to crash to land

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.062
into not land rather crash

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:38.398
into the Black Sea a total loss U.S.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.065
officials say.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:41.134
But Moscow says this is simply not true.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.268
They deny that there was

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.736
any physical contact

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.271
between one of their fighter jets.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.674
And if you ask me, drone Russia says

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:48.741
in fact, that it

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.111
detected an intruder over

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.112
the Black Sea waters.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.880
It scrambled its fighter jets

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.615
that that drone, the U.S.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.851
Army drone, did not have its transponders

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.619
on which Russia says is a violation

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.788
of international standards and norms.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.155
In fact,

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:02.655
Russia says

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:03.456
it had warned

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.024
that it was operating in the air,

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.392
that it was carrying out

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.561
its special military operations

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.097
in that Black Sea area and had warned

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.799
about that action

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.634
and in fact, blames the United States.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.935
Pointing fingers at the US,

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.070
says it's America

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.372
that was behaving recklessly, dangerously

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:20.940
in the Black Sea.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.041
One Kremlin spokesman

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.343
saying that relationships

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:23.877
between Russia

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.179
and the United States are deplorable

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.314
now that they're at an all time low.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.183
Now, one positive sign

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.784
is that both sides seem to agree

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.653
that this should not escalate

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:34.420
any further.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.122
Russia's ambassador to D.C.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.957
to the United States was summoned.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.826
There was about a 30 minute meeting there

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.894
in the State Department.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.495
He called it constructive.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.230
So for now, it seems that

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.965
neither party wants to see this escalate.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.367
But all eyes on the Black Sea

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.168
as to whether or not

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.702
the Americans can somehow.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.770
And it's impossible to imagine

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.905
that this could take place,

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:52.939
could somehow

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:53.740
get the remnants

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.008
of that drone from the Black Sea.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.276
But important to note, of course,

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.911
Russia very much operates

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.613
in that flashpoint area of the Black Sea.

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.483
Some.
Abdulaziz, thank you for joining us.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.018
Colin Edwards at the State Department.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.520
Ivan Watson is in eastern Ukraine.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.156
And you're there monitoring

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.891
not just what's going on the ground,

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.294
but the response on this incident

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:16.196
from the Kremlin. What's been said

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.732
Well, we've

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.000
seen the first official response

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.168
from the Ukrainian government

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.036
to this incident

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:23.870
in the Black Sea,

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.605
and not much of a surprise

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.706
given how

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:30.009
closely allied Kiev and Washington are.

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.278
The head of the National Security

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:32.679
and Defense

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:36.482
Council has called Russia's alleged

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.818
downing of this American Air Force drone

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.154
a provocation

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.189
and said that this indicates

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.757
Putin's readiness

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.993
to expand the conflict zone

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:49.629
with the involvement of other parties.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.864
So we're standing very much

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.933
behind the U.S. on this.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.469
Again, not much of a surprise.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.906
The Russians have claimed

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:00.907
that no weapons

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:03.009
were used to force down this U.S.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.477
Air Force Reaper

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:07.513
and that there was no conflict tact

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.917
between the Russian fighter jets

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.518
and the drone itself,

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.353
which is something

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.421
that the Pentagon is disputing.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.189
Now, I want to turn

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.123
your attention, Becky,

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.092
to another incident

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:19.859
that took place

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:20.727
just to show you

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.761
how frequent

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.330
these types of aerial intercepts are.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:27.600
This is over Estonia where

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.870
a British and German warplane

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.539
were scrambled to intercept

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:36.909
and then escort a Russian military plane

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.979
over Estonia after the.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.516
The Royal Air Force says that

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.851
the Russian

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.552
plane did not respond

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.621
to air traffic control.

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.323
This is apparently a Russian

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.157
refueling plane

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:51.891
that was flying

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.826
between the Russian enclave

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.462
of Kaliningrad and St Petersburg.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.598
There were no collisions here.

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.667
This is a standard practice

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.969
that we see practiced around the world.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.271
But something went very wrong

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.306
in the Black Sea

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.142
and had raised tensions there Becky.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.844
Well, Ivan, thank you.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.680
Let's get to the State Department then.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.016
What do we understand happened?

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.017
Well, listen, what U.S.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:18.918
officials are saying

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:19.952
is that, first of all,

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:20.253
there were

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.021
two Russian aircraft

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.390
that poured fuel onto this drone,

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.291
and then

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.392
that there was

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.661
one of the Russian aircrafts aircraft

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.264
who actually intercepted the U.S. drone.

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:33.099
And that's what led to it going down.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.233
So they're being pretty clear

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:34.901
in saying

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.070
that this was a very risky

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.872
and very aggressive action by Russia.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:40.840
Now, one

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.574
interesting thing

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.542
that we learned this morning

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.476
from John Kirby

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.311
from the National Security Council

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:45.945
at the White House

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.214
is that
there is some footage of this incident

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.582
actually occurring.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.517
The Pentagon has that footage.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:52.652
We're waiting to see

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.820
if the Biden administration

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.421
decides to make that footage public,

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.023
because that could provide

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.524
a very clear accounting

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:01.160
potentially of what actually went down.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.795
And what we also heard from Kirby

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:03.663
this morning

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:05.765
was that what the US has done is

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:06.799
take steps

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:07.467
to make sure

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:09.669
that any of the information that are on

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.237
that drone is protected.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.805
They can obviously do that remotely

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:13.706
because it's a drone

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.274
that's remotely operated.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.275
But what he also said

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.243
is that they're not sure

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.277
if they're actually going to be able

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.979
to recover this drone

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.514
because it's just so far

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.583
in the depths of the Black Sea right now.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.985
So that is a point for us to also watch.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:28.121
We heard from the secretary of defense

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.522
this morning, Lloyd Austin,

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.324
who talked about the incident

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.092
and how it's not going to prevent

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:33.926
the U.S.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:34.994
from flying these drones

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.863
in international airspace is going forth.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:37.797
Listen to what he said.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:39.799
I know

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:42.902
that everyone here has heard that

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.203
Russian aircraft, again

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.339
engaged in dangerous,

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:49.041
reckless and unprofessional practices

00:06:49.142 --> 00:06:50.710
on Tuesday

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.211
in international airspace

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.080
over the Black Sea.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.183
Two Russian jets dumped fuel

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.851
on an unmanned U.S.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:00.453
MQ nine aircraft

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.255
conducting routine operations

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:05.024
in international airspace.

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:07.360
And one Russian jet intercepted and hit

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.562
our MQ nine aircraft

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:12.331
resulting in a crash.

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:14.434
This hazardous episode

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.769
is a part of a pattern

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:18.738
of aggressive

00:07:18.738 --> 00:07:21.040
and risky and unsafe actions

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:22.875
by Russian pilots

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:25.445
in international airspace.

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:27.613
So make no mistake,

00:07:27.647 --> 00:07:29.982
the United States will continue to fly

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.050
and to operate

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.820
wherever international law allows.

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:36.889
And it is incumbent upon Russia

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.692
to operate its military aircraft

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:43.563
in a safe and professional manner.

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:44.964
Now, what we've also heard from U.S.

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:45.465
officials

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:46.532
is that incidents

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:47.934
like this increase

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:49.836
the risk of miscount dilation.

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:51.337
And the concern here is that

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:53.673
there could be more confrontation

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:55.675
between the US and Russia.

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:57.877
Beyond this, of course, the Ukraine war.

00:07:57.877 --> 00:08:00.179
But between the two nations directly

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:01.714
and that is the concern here.

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:02.782
What we're waiting to see

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.951
is the full extent of the U.S. response.

00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:07.019
Obviously, we have seen them condemning

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:07.920
what happened.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.689
Condemning Russia's aggression.

00:08:09.689 --> 00:08:10.523
But we're waiting to see

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:11.924
if there's more to come

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:12.992
from the Biden administration.

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:16.896
And on the part of the Kremlin,

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.131
the spokesperson is saying,

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:21.334
and I quote, The US and Russia

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:22.935
relations are in a, quote,

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.804
deplorable state

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:26.739
and at their lowest point.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:27.974
Another quote, adding that

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:28.808
Russian President

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:29.942
Vladimir Putin

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:32.144
was briefed on the incident.

00:08:33.246 --> 00:08:34.046
Always a pleasure.

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:35.181
Thank you very much indeed.

